<title>YEMEN: British Airways offered Yemen landing rights.</title>
<headline>British Airways offered Yemen landing rights.</headline>
<dateline>SANAA 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yemeni President Ali Abdullah Saleh on Wednesday offered British Airways landing rights in Sanaa and Aden, British officials said.</p>
<p>The president made the offer in &quot;recognition of the Foreign Secretary's visit&quot;, a British official said.</p>
<p>Foreign Secretary Malcolm Rifkind arrived in Yemen on Tuesday on the last leg of a regional tour of the Middle East.</p>
<p>Until now British Airways had only been offered landing rights in Sanaa. The airline had not taken up the offer, because it had argued that without being able to land in both Sanaa and Aden, it was not a financially viable option.</p>
</text>
